2. The solution: groupBy().agg(median())
========================================================================
+--------+----------+------------+
|zip_code|homes_sold|median_price|
+--------+----------+------------+
|   95014|         4|      3000.0|
|   95050|         5|      1310.0|
|   95112|         3|      1050.0|
+--------+----------+------------+

95014 has 4 sales: its median is (2900 + 3100) / 2 = 3000.0.
(median() always returns a double.)

The report the website shows:
  95014 (Cupertino)   4 homes sold   median price: $3,000K
  95050 (Santa Clara)   5 homes sold   median price: $1,310K
  95112 (San Jose)   3 homes sold   median price: $1,050K

