========================================================================
5. A common mistake: percentile_approx() is not the median
========================================================================
+--------+------+-----------------+
|zip_code|median|percentile_approx|
+--------+------+-----------------+
|   95014|3000.0|             2900|
|   95050|1310.0|             1310|
|   95112|1050.0|             1050|
+--------+------+-----------------+

For 95014 (4 sales), percentile_approx() says 2900, not 3000.0:
  1. it never averages: it returns an ACTUAL value from the data (the
     smallest price with at least half of the prices <= it);
  2. it is approximate: it keeps a small fixed-size sketch per group,
     not every value (error controlled by its 'accuracy' argument).
Point 2 is also its strength: sketches merge like partial sums, so it
works on groups of ANY size. Use median() for an exact median when each
group fits in memory; percentile_approx() for huge groups.
